From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:23:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: mtu3: power down at runtime only with a wake
 path

The runtime PM callbacks power the controller, its PHY and clocks down
only when device_may_wakeup(), because once down nothing but the
IP-sleep wakeup or a wakeup interrupt brings it back for a host
connecting or a cable attached. Probe sets the device as wakeup-enabled
unconditionally, which defeats that check on a controller with neither.

On the Gemini (no wakeup-source, no wakeup interrupt, and a PHY that
forces the B-session valid so no VBUS change is seen), the controller
runtime-suspended once a suspend's reconnection had dropped the last
reference, and a replug was never noticed: the gadget stayed "not
attached" until userspace cycled soft_connect, whose pullup call
resumes the device.

Enable wakeup only when a wake path is configured. Without one the
controller stays powered and keeps watching the bus.
---
 drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
index 461575310..fb88fbdb7 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/mtu3/mtu3_plat.c
@@ -358,7 +358,13 @@ static int mtu3_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
 
-	device_init_wakeup(dev, true);
+	/*
+	 * The runtime callbacks power the controller down only for a device
+	 * that may wake, since nothing else would bring it back for a host or
+	 * a cable. Claim that only with a wake path: the IP-sleep wakeup or a
+	 * wakeup interrupt.
+	 */
+	device_init_wakeup(dev, ssusb->uwk_en || ssusb->wakeup_irq > 0);
 
 	ret = ssusb_rscs_init(ssusb);
 	if (ret)
-- 
